    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d128">

                <pb facs="0245" n="145" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg145"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.60d31/78: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Finland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Albright</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Helsingfors</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-08-11T10:00:00+02:00">August 11, 1934—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 11—6:34 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your telegram No. 21, Aug. 6, 6 [<hi rendition="#italic">3</hi>] p.m. reached
                    Legation following call Mr. Sayre on Acting Finnish Minister for Foreign
                        Affairs<anchor n="22" xml:id="d128-f1"/> and he wishes that the Department
                    know it and that he approved of Legation requesting Foreign Office for decision.
                    Acting Finnish Minister for Foreign Affairs states that experts will probably be
                    sent to Washington for exploratory conversations but that official decision will
                    not be made until the question submitted to Cabinet next week.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Albright</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d128-f1" n="22" xml:id="d128-f1-content">
                <p>Rolf Witting.</p>
